        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "41a0518d-25ee-57cf-a311-0a0656311c30",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants/Genera: Colocasia, Coronilla, Xanthosoma, Caladium, Alocasia\n- Places: southeastern Asia, Indian subcontinent, Europe, North Africa, Lampazos, Nuevo León\n- Concepts: flowering plants, ornamental plants, elephant ear\n\nFacts:\n- Colocasia is a genus of flowering plants in the family Araceae that is native to southeastern Asia and the Indian subcontinent.\n- Coronilla is a genus of about 20 species of flowering plants native to Europe and North Africa.\n- Xanthosoma species, especially Xanthosoma roseum, are used as ornamental plants and are called ape or elephant ear in popular horticultural literature.\n- The name elephant ear is also applied to similar plants in the related genera Caladium, Colocasia, and Alocasia.\n- Lampazos, Nuevo León, is named in part after the local plant Xanthosoma robustum, which is called lampazos in Spanish.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "4d1c7e59-00bc-5659-baa1-177244fce3b0",
        "text": "Page: Colocasia. Sentence: Colocasia is a genus of flowering plants in the family Araceae, native to southeastern Asia and the Indian subcontinent.\nPage: Coronilla. Sentence: The genus Coronilla contains about 20 species of flowering plants native to Europe and North Africa.\nPage: Xanthosoma. Sentence: Many other species (including especially \"X. roseum\") are used as ornamental plants, and in popular horticultural literature are known as ‘ape or elephant ear (from the purported resemblance of the leaf to an elephant's ear), although the latter name is sometimes also applied to members with similar appearance and uses in the closely related genera \"Caladium\", \"Colocasia\" (i.e., taro), and \"Alocasia\".\nPage: Lampazos, Nuevo León. Sentence: Its name is composed of two parts: the first honors a local plant: Xanthosoma Robustum called \"Lampazos\" in Spanish.",
